.\" fsck_ufsbe.8
.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd September 11, 2026
.Dt FSCK_UFSBE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fsck_ufsbe
.Nd check and repair a ufsbe filesystem
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl dfnpy
.Ar special
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
checks and repairs a UFS2 filesystem that has the
.Dv FS_BETREE
flag
.Pq 0x00000800
set in its superblock.
Such a filesystem stores per-inode block maps as B-epsilon trees in
.Va di_extb[0]
and directory indexes in
.Va di_extb[1]
rather than using the standard
.Va di_db[]
and
.Va di_ib[]
fields.
.Pp
.Nm
refuses to run on a filesystem without
.Dv FS_BETREE
set; use
.Xr fsck_ffs 8
for standard UFS filesystems.
Do not run
.Xr fsck_ffs 8
on a
.Dv FS_BETREE
filesystem.
.Ss Checking phases
.Bl -tag -width "Phase 0"
.It Phase 0
Read and validate the superblock.
Confirm
.Dv FS_BETREE
is set.
.It Phase 1
Walk every allocated inode.
For each inode:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Verify
.Va di_db[]
and
.Va di_ib[]
are all zero.
.It
Traverse the B-epsilon blkmap tree
.Pq Va di_extb[0]
and verify node magic, key sort order, and block number range.
Check for duplicate block references across all inodes.
.It
Traverse the B-epsilon directory-index tree
.Pq Va di_extb[1]
for directory inodes.
.It
Recount referenced blocks and compare to
.Va di_blocks ;
correct if mismatched.
.El
.It Phase 2
Scan directory data blocks
.Pq linear Vt struct direct
for invalid
.Va d_reclen
or oversized
.Va d_namlen
values.
.It Phase 5
Compare the cylinder-group free-block bitmaps against the set of
blocks actually referenced by inodes.
Report blocks marked free but in use.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl d
Enable debug output.
.It Fl f
Force check even if the filesystem is marked clean.
.It Fl n
Assume
.Dq no
to all repair prompts
.Pq read-only check .
.It Fl p
Preen: fix errors automatically without prompting.
.It Fl y
Assume
.Dq yes
to all repair prompts.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Exit code 0 means the filesystem is clean or all errors were fixed.
Exit code 8 means errors remain that could not be fixed.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check a filesystem preen-style:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# fsck_ufsbe -p /dev/md0
.Ed
.Pp
Force a full check even if clean:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# fsck_ufsbe -f /dev/md0
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ufsbe 8 ,
.Xr newfs_ufsbe 8 ,
.Xr fsck_ffs 8 ,
.Xr libufs 3
